{"schema":2,"commit":"6499f380dbc6b2e9488c33028f45c85c3fe6fb5e","branch":"fix/windows-update-handoff","base_sha":"34fa59de24a2e682c08be77c675b01711a821780","message":"Make the Windows auto-update survive its own hand-off\nThe daemon's auto-update failed on Windows with `fork/exec ...: the\nrequest is not supported` (ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED). The staged binary had\nrun fine seconds earlier for the `--version` sanity gate, on the same\npath — the difference was how each child was started. binaryVersion uses\nCombinedOutput, so os/exec gives the child pipes; runInstaller assigned\nos.Stdin/os.Stdout/os.Stderr.\nA process started with CREATE_NO_WINDOW, from a Scheduled Task or from a\nStartup shortcut, has no standard handles, but the os package still\nwraps whatever GetStdHandle returned. syscall.StartProcess sets\nSTARTF_USESTDHANDLES unconditionally and duplicates every handle it\nconsiders non-zero; INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE is the current-process\npseudo-handle, so the duplicate succeeds and CreateProcess is handed a\nPROCESS handle where it expects a file or pipe.\nrunInstaller now inherits nothing: stdin stays nil (the installer never\nreads it — BLAMELY_INSTALL_YES covers its one prompt) and stdout/stderr\nfollow the caller's Out, with an unusable *os.File dropped rather than\npassed on (usableStdHandle, stdio_windows.go).\nUpdate also stops depending on that hand-off for the update itself. It\nnow places the new binary at the stable path first, by rename —\nCopyBinary/placeBinary already move a locked Windows image aside as\n\u003cname\u003e.old-\u003cts\u003e and roll back on failure. Every caller of blamely spells\nthat stable path (each tool hook, the git hook, the autostart entry, the\nkeepalive task) and none of them is rewritten by an update, so swapping\nthe file behind it IS the update; nothing else has to succeed for the new\nversion to take over at the next start. The hand-off keeps its remaining\njob — refreshing hooks and restarting the agent — as best effort, which\nmatters because it is a CHILD of this process and `blamely install` kills\nthis process's tree on Windows. The sanity gate still runs first, so what\ngets placed is known to execute and report the expected version.\n\nReview follow-ups: derive the child's writer once and assign the same\nvalue to both streams, so os/exec keeps them on a single pipe rather than\ncopying two separately-derived values concurrently; correct the stdin\ncomment, which claimed the installer never reads stdin and cited an env\nvar that lives in the installer script, not here; and stop the JetBrains\nplugin-locked retry from looping forever on an empty stdin. That loop is\ngated by stdinInteractive(), which tests for a character device — and\nWindows reports NUL as one, so a hand-off child could reach the prompt,\nread EOF, match no case and reprint it endlessly. A read error now ends\nthe loop. The passthrough test uses a temp file instead of os.Stdout,\nwhich is itself the unusable case on a Windows host with no console.","coding_time_nanos":60733649000,"totals":{"added_lines":296,"ai_added_lines":248,"human_added_lines":48,"deleted_lines":17,"ai_deleted_lines":0,"human_deleted_lines":17,"files":6,"tokens":{"input":4,"output":6608,"cache_read":1187242,"cache_write":3200},"models":{"claude-opus-5":248}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":248,"suggested_lines":1285,"accepted_lines":248,"tokens":{"input":4,"output":6608,"cache_read":1187242,"cache_write":3200}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":248,"cli":0,"completion":0,"human":65},"files":[{"path":"internal/install/jetbrainsplugin.go","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":8,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":8,"lines":[{"start":467,"end":474,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"chat"}]},{"path":"internal/install/stdio_other.go","type":"ADDED","added_lines":13,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":13,"lines":[{"start":1,"end":13,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":